                <head>PM–61. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On October 1, 1960, Dr. Roberto Chiari, the victor in Panama’s presidential
                    elections held on May 8, 1960, was sworn in as President of Panama for a
                    four-year term. In his inaugural speech President Chiari expressed gratification
                    at the United States’ recognition of Panama’s titular sovereignty over the
                    Panama Canal Zone, but at the same time he maintained that the United States had
                    not complied fully with the terms of the treaties covering Canal Zone
                    operations. He was optimistic, however, that the United States’ recognition of
                    Panama’s titular sovereignty foreshadowed a new era of good relations that would
                    enable the two nations to find practical solutions to existing problems.
                    Documentation concerning President Chiari’s inauguration is in decimal file
                    719.11.</p>
            </div>
